DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       This program is part of NNeettppbbmm(1).

       zzeeiissssttooppnnmm  reads a Zeiss confocal file as input and produces a PNM im‐
       age as output.

       By default, the exact type of the output depends on the input file:  If
       it's  grayscale  a  PGM  image; otherwise a PPM.  The program tells you
       which type it is writing.  You can override the default with  the  --ppggmm
       and --ppppmm options.



OOPPTTIIOONNSS
       In  addition  to  the options common to all programs based on libnetpbm
       (most notably --qquuiieett, see
        Common Options ⟨index.html#commonoptions⟩ ), zzeeiissssttooppnnmm recognizes the
       following command line options:



       --ppggmm   Force the output to be in PGM format.


       --ppppmm   Force the output to be in PPM format.




